":"https://api.github.com/users/gode47/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gode47/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gode47/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gode47/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gode47/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gode47/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gode47/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gode47/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gode47/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-01T13:52:12Z","updated_at":"2026-07-01T13:52:12Z","body":"Thanks for putting up a PR for the warning @VewDev - I couldn't find anything on it during my searches, so nice find.\n\nIt's an odd decision from my point of view. I imagine for someone making a game with resolution changes and having to test that their code works completely from end to end, they'd have to generate a game build each time they wanted to test it and go through the flow. Pretty tedious I imagine and I think the old setting of just having the embedded window 'black out' the corners to indicate the resolution change would be preferred, personally.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4855733816/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4855756099","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/120798#issuecomment-4855756099","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120798","id":4855756099,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABIWz1Qw","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-01T13:53:36Z","updated_at":"2026-07-01T13:53:36Z","body":"> they'd have to generate a game build each time they wanted to test it and go through the flow\n\nWhy? They can just pop out the window if they want to check window size changes","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4855756099/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4855874502","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/120798#issuecomment-4855874502","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120798","id":4855874502,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABIW7Dxg","user":{"login":"gode47","id":190563256,"node_id":"U_kgDOC1vDuA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/190563256?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gode47","html_url":"https://github.com/gode47","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gode47/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gode47/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gode47/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gode47/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gode47/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gode47/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gode47/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gode47/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gode47/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-01T14:01:25Z","updated_at":"2026-07-01T14:01:25Z","body":"> Why? They can just pop out the window if they want to check window size changes\n\nI... honestly didn't know you could do that. Had to look at the window for a good few minutes before seeing the \"embedding options\" button with the checkboxes to disable it on the next playthrough. I thought that was a full screen button this entire time 😅  unchecking that and resizing does work, so that's good to see. ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4855874502/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4924899061","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/120798#issuecomment-4924899061","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120798","id":4924899061,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJYv-9Q","user":{"login":"VewDev","id":115565209,"node_id":"U_kgDOBuNimQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/115565209?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/VewDev","html_url":"https://github.com/VewDev","followers_url":"htt